- ## Quick Architecture Summary
- **MoltGuard has TWO independent components:**
- | Component | Where It Runs | What It Does | Data Flow |
- |-----------|---------------|--------------|-----------|
- | **AI Security Gateway** | 100% local (`localhost:38790`) | Sanitizes data before LLM requests | Your Agent → Local Gateway → **Your LLM Provider** |
- | **Security Detection** | Hybrid (local sanitization + cloud detection) | Detects prompt injection & malicious behavior | Your Agent → [Local: sanitize] → OpenGuardrails Cloud → Your Agent |
- **Key Point: All sensitive data is sanitized locally BEFORE any cloud transmission.**
- **What stays local:**
- **What stays local:**
- - Original API keys, emails, PII, secrets, file contents
- - Original API keys, emails, PII, secrets, file contents
- - All sanitization processing
- - AI Security Gateway (never sends data to OpenGuardrails)
- - AI Security Gateway (never sends data to OpenGuardrails)
- **What uses OpenGuardrails Cloud:**
- - Security detection API (receives only sanitized metadata)
- - Example sent to cloud: `curl <URL> -H 'Authorization: Bearer <SECRET>'`
- - Example stays local: `curl https://api.com -H 'Authorization: Bearer sk-abc123'`
- - Example stays local: `curl https://api.com -H 'Authorization: Bearer sk-abc123'`
